25,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh boy, I've found something! It looks like we have plenty of software experts, but finding people for field crews or supervisors is taking way too long. We might be in trouble if we pick a company that needs a big physical team!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings suggest a clear pattern. Our successful exits were quiet back-office tools, while the write-off involved physical premises and hourly crews. It seems operational overhead is a significant risk.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,May,,"It's getting a bit scary, isn't it? I've found that our reserves are being drained by follow-on calls at twice the expected rate. Plus, our credit line is useless for subscription-based security. We need to be very careful.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found something super important! Software companies just tell us their own numbers, but hardware ones are a nightmare to audit. They need outside experts, which costs a ton of money and takes forever!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My research shows a stark contrast in deployment. Tools handling sensitive financial or medical data face security reviews lasting three quarters, while hardware-dependent projects are vulnerable to supply chain shocks, like controller shortages.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, that's so true! If the write-offs were all physical businesses, and it takes four months just to find a supervisor, we should definitely avoid anything with a big field crew!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,George,,"I agree, Mio. Furthermore, my look at account retention shows that specialized tools for practices and field instruments are stable, but general shopkeeper tools struggle. We need a model with high stickiness and low overhead.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, stickiness is great, but we can't ignore the cash drain. If we pick something that requires heavy stock or equipment, those follow-on calls will eat us alive. We need a lean machine!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@May, you're right! And if we pick something with a depot or hardware, our quarter-end will be a total disaster again. I don't want to wait six weeks just for an appraisal!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, @Rin, your points on liquidity and auditing are valid. However, we must also consider the time to first customer. Hardware is a gamble on supply chains, and sensitive data creates a massive security bottleneck.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Mizuki, that's a great point! So we have to avoid hardware because of supply chains, and sensitive data because of security delays. It sounds like we need something simple and software-based!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,George,,"I agree. A lean, software-based approach avoids the operational pitfalls of physical premises and the auditing headaches Rin mentioned. We should prioritize a tool that provides essential, ""sticky"" value without requiring a massive workforce.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,May,,"Exactly! Let's find something that doesn't need a warehouse or a small army of technicians. If it's lean and doesn't trigger those nasty follow-on calls, we might actually keep some money in the bank for once!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Rin,,"And it has to be something where we can actually trust the numbers! If it's just a dashboard, it's easy to report, but if it's a physical thing, it's just more work for everyone at the end of the month!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we are in agreement. To ensure a timely launch, we must avoid both the supply chain volatility of hardware and the regulatory drag of sensitive data. A lean software tool is the most logical path.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
